                <pb facs="0744" n="716" xml:id="pg716"/>

                <head>294. Memorandum From the Director of the Policy Planning Staff (Kennan) to the Under Secretary of
                    State (Lovett)<anchor n="0"
                        xml:id="d294-f1"/></head>
                <dateline><placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                        when="1948-06-30">June 30, 1948</date>.</dateline>
                <p>The following are my suggestions, in the order named, for persons whom the
                    Secretary could nominate as Chief of the Office of Special Projects under the
                    Central Intelligence Agency: <list>
                        <item>Frank Wisner</item>
                        <item>Mathias F. Correa</item>
                        <item>Irving Brown (representative of A.F. of L. in
                            Paris and a very able and active citizen)</item>
                        <item>Norris Chipman (Foreign Service Officer in
                            Paris)</item>
                        <item>Francis Stevens (now Chief of the Russian
                            Division)</item>
                        <item>John Davies (member of my Staff)</item>
                    </list></p>
                <p>I am told there is little likelihood of getting Correa. I have no information as to Brown’s
                    availability and feel that this would have to be considered a political
                    appointment to be discussed first with William Green.</p>
                <p>I have placed Wisner at the head of the
                    list on the recommendations of people who know him. I personally have no
                    knowledge of his ability, but his qualifications seem reasonably good, and I
                    should think that it would be relatively easy to spare him for this purpose.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#bold">George F. Kennan</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
